  (text "B4 — ISOLATED SWITCHING: 4 x SPDT relay (3 A / 30 VDC) on AO3400A MOSFETs; 2 x 6N137 isolated inputs, 5-24 V" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 14 0) (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a4b368d5-9c44-52cc-aac8-f02784972b6a"))
  (text "Relay drive: AO3400A (48 mOhm) instead of a Darlington: the 5 V coil gets the full +5V_RAW (HK4100F pull-in <= 3.75 V guaranteed, coil 125 R = 40 mA). 1 k gate series, 1N4148W flyback across the coil. Yellow LED shows coil on." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 19 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b29f4436-ee4c-5bf2-ba2d-2bde1abe20de"))
  (text "v0.7: the gates are driven by RLY_IN1..4 from the TCA9535 I2C expander (B5, address 0x20), not by a GPIO. The 10 k gate pull-down is what keeps every relay OFF while the ESP32 boots and while the expander powers up with all its ports as inputs (high-impedance) — it must not be omitted." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 22.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e14e4c64-e858-5a17-b2f5-d7ce968121c4"))
  (text "Contacts: COM/NO/NC to a 3P terminal. Rated 3 A at 30 VDC / 250 VAC by the relay, but this board is limited to <= 30 V DC, 1 A (silkscreen). NO = pad 1, NC = pad 2, COM = pads 5/6 (HK4100F drawing, bottom view mirrored)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 25.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b2d24a17-5c5a-5536-9050-6471f44bdcf1"))
  (text "Isolated input: series 1N4148W (reverse blocking) -> 220 R -> Q1 pass transistor with Q2 sensing 0.65 V across Rs (100 R || 1 k = 91 R): LED current ~6.5-7 mA from 5 V to 24 V (6N137 needs 5-15 mA). At 24 V Q1 dissipates ~125 mW (MMBT5551 300 mW)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 28.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a4eaa835-d7bc-56db-98db-fae30c107367"))
  (text "6N137: VCC/VE = +3V3, 1 k pull-up; output LOW when the input is driven (inverting). The isolated side nets (ISO1_*, ISO2_*) have a 2.5 mm clearance class and no copper of any other net underneath." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 31.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9c5603f6-605c-5eb2-abdf-937d6d03851d"))
  (text "J401: 1 = NO, 2 = COM, 3 = NC   (<= 30 V DC, 1 A)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 45 132 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1824898f-1571-536b-b786-61d56e77403a"))
  (text "J402: 1 = NO, 2 = COM, 3 = NC   (<= 30 V DC, 1 A)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 135 132 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6377165a-a8eb-5071-8010-678d972c253b"))
  (text "J403: 1 = NO, 2 = COM, 3 = NC   (<= 30 V DC, 1 A)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 225 132 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1442423a-ec1e-5dd2-ba0f-87510fa235ff"))
  (text "J404: 1 = NO, 2 = COM, 3 = NC   (<= 30 V DC, 1 A)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 315 132 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6aa03e54-bd8e-50f7-a427-3f4ab8125c6f"))
  (text "v0.7 gate drive: RLY_IN1..4 = TCA9535 P10..P13 (expander U505 on B5, I2C address 0x20) through the 1 k series resistor; the 10 k pull-down holds every relay off at boot and while the expander ports are still inputs." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 40 142 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ec93cf43-d015-5ceb-875c-20695a2fa561"))
  (text "J411: 1 = IN+, 2 = IN- (5-24 V DC, isolated, 1.5 kV opto)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 40 270 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "062e4320-23b4-5a28-9648-becadf97d3d4"))
